<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8928" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθυπ-άγω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰγ</span>], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bring to trial</i> or <i>indict in turn,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.70
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>rejoin, reply,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				53.21
			</span></i>, al.:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ-αγόμενον, -αχθησόμενον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				118.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				121.22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>substitute,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				12.9
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>lead under in turn,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰχμαλώτους ὑπὸ τὸ ζυγόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					36.22
				</span></i>
			; but in 
				Med.
			, <i>bring over,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰς ἐς εὔνοιαν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				35.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>withdraw in turn,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθυπῆγε Μαρδόνιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.
					1.146J.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
